headset: disable what is still on before putting it

sprd_headset_regulator_init() turns CLK_DCL_32K and DIG_CLK_INTC on when the
codec's component probes ("enable these all the time after bootup") and nothing
turns them off again: sprd_headset_power_deinit(), which runs when the component
is removed, put both while they were still enabled. Every unbind of the card -
mu300-audio-dsp rebinds it when it finds it unregistered - therefore logged

  WARNING: ... at drivers/regulator/core.c:2173 _regulator_put+0x104/0x114
   regulator_put
   sprd_headset_power_deinit [snd_soc_sprd_codec_ump9620]
   sprd_headset_remove
   sprd_codec_soc_remove
   snd_soc_component_remove ... snd_soc_unregister_card ... unbind_store

twice (one per regulator; WARN_ON(regulator->enable_count), "Docs say you must
disable before calling regulator_put()"). The enable count of the regulator
itself leaked with each, and 'en' stayed true, so the next probe's
sprd_headset_power_set(..., true) took the new handle as already on and never
enabled it.

Disable each one that is on before it is put, and clear 'en'.

--- a/sprd/codec/sprd/ump9620/codec/sprd-headset-ump9620.c
+++ b/sprd/codec/sprd/ump9620/codec/sprd-headset-ump9620.c
@@ -285,6 +285,21 @@
 	while (i < HDST_REGULATOR_COUNT) {
 		power_temp = &power[i++];
 		if (power_temp->hdst_regu) {
+			/*
+			 * MU300: sprd_headset_regulator_init() keeps CLK_DCL_32K and
+			 * DIG_CLK_INTC on for as long as the codec is probed, and this
+			 * put them while still enabled: a WARN in _regulator_put()
+			 * (core.c, "Docs say you must disable before calling
+			 * regulator_put()") for each whenever the card was unbound
+			 * (mu300-audio-dsp rebinds it), the enable leaked, and 'en'
+			 * stayed true, so the next probe never enabled the new handle.
+			 */
+			if (power_temp->en) {
+				pr_info("%s: %s still enabled, disabled before put\n",
+					__func__, power_temp->name);
+				regulator_disable(power_temp->hdst_regu);
+				power_temp->en = false;
+			}
 			regulator_put(power_temp->hdst_regu);
 			power_temp->hdst_regu = NULL;
 			power_temp->name = NULL;
